senses.gloss:
शकुन शक् + उन (or rather शक् + वन् + अ, cf. शकुन्त),
 I. m. A bird, Nal. 9, 12.
 II. n. An omen;
 a. auspicious, Lass. 43, 5;
 b. inauspicious, Pañc. 52, 11 (किं शकुनकारनं किं चित् संजातम्, Has something come to pass caused by a bird, or by an inauspicious omen, i. e. has there happened a misfortune?).
 --Comp.
